---
onetaskgraph_template: 1
description: >-
  The plan that grooms the follow-ups board through onefollowup: prepare the open tickets to
  verify, run one verifying dispatch per shard, check every verdict, and publish what the
  check planned, reading back every changed ticket and writing the report. `just groom`
  creates it and runs it in a flow.
variables:
  project:
    description: The plan's native id, which every member's own id is prefixed with.
    type: string
    required: true
members:
  - id: "{{ project }}-prepare"
    title: "Prepare the open follow-up tickets to verify"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "List the destination's open tickets, fetch their repositories and write one task per shard of the tickets to verify with `onefollowup groom prepare`."}
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: prepare
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [just, groom, --prepare]
  - id: "{{ project }}-verify"
    title: "Verify the prepared tickets, one verifying run per shard"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "For each shard `onefollowup groom prepare` named, create its verifying plan from the shard's task and run it attached in this flow."}
    depends_on: ["{{ project }}-prepare"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: verify
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [just, groom, --verify]
  - id: "{{ project }}-check"
    title: "Check every shard's verdicts"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "Hold every verdict to the rules and plan what publish sends with `onefollowup groom check`."}
    depends_on: ["{{ project }}-verify"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: check
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [just, groom, --check]
  - id: "{{ project }}-publish"
    title: "Publish the checked plan and write the report"
    template: {file: follow-up-step.md.j2}
    answers: {step: "Send what the check planned, read back every changed ticket and write the batch's report with `onefollowup groom publish`."}
    depends_on: ["{{ project }}-check"]
    metadata:
      onepipeline.id: publish
      onepipeline.kind: command
      onepipeline.command: [just, groom, --publish]
---
Groom this host's follow-ups board through onefollowup: close what is fixed, obsolete or a
duplicate, and record what every verified ticket was verified against.
